        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12354848/comment/12465732",
          "id": "12465732",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "I did have a look at this before Christmas but I only have a partial fix to this. Fixing this properly requires tracking a bit more information than is currently used and deciding what (if anything) to do with live sessions that get broken by the underlying remote repository disappearing.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2007-01-18T11:37:39.900+0000",
          "updated": "2007-01-18T11:37:39.900+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12354848/comment/12477974",
          "id": "12477974",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=c_koell",
            "name": "c_koell",
            "key": "c_koell",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Claus K\u00f6ll",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Hi Jukka,\nDo you have more Informations about broken sessions ?\nWhat partial fix do you have ? I need some fix for this issue, because we can not go into production\nuntil this issue is fixed. We are in a Model 3 Deployment and our (Client)Applications have the WebDAVServlet\nwhich connects to a RMI Repository Server. If this Server now restart all client applications must restartet.\nHope for fix\nclaus",
